WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.080
From Goth to rainbow, via the&nbsp;
grisliest crimes the U.S. Navy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.980
has ever faced — who else but NCIS' Abby Sciuto?

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.720
Abby Sciuto's style, as seen on&nbsp;
NCIS from Season 1 to Season 15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.040
often seems to clash with her chipper&nbsp;
personality, but this forensic scientist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.980
is ultimately a goth at heart. After all, Abby&nbsp;
loves not just death, but the supernatural,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.720
tattoos, and black clothes and jewelry,&nbsp;
too. Maybe that's why Abby became a fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.640
favorite in short order — it's certainly what&nbsp;
the minds behind the character were aiming for.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.500
Part of executive producer Donald&nbsp;
Bellisario's intent with Abby was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.900
to create a positive depiction of a person&nbsp;
with tattoos and piercings. Perrette told CBS:

00:00:51.987 --> 00:00:55.500
She also discussed how many girls&nbsp;
followed in her character's footsteps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.300
taking up math and science courses in&nbsp;
college because Abby made these topics fun.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.420
Outside of work, Abby is a competent, plucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.240
and kind-hearted human being. And part of her&nbsp;
now-iconic ensemble is her striking black hair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.560
which she typically fashions into&nbsp;
pigtails with bangs. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.120
though, that hair color isn't the shade&nbsp;
that actor Pauley Perrette was born with.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.860
Over the years, Pauley Perrette's jet black&nbsp;
locks may have become one of the trademarks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.980
of Abby Sciuto on NCIS, but the actor's hair is&nbsp;
actually blonde. To pull off her look as Abby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:33.120
Perrette regularly dyed it black with&nbsp;
the help of hair and make-up assistants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.440
who also gave her a hand applying&nbsp;
Abby's neck tattoo before filming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.360
began each day. She once told CBS Sunday&nbsp;
Morning that, while working on the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:48.120
she actually ended up with dyed roots.&nbsp;
Furthermore, the actor tweeted in 2013:

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.520
However, Perrette revealed on The Queen&nbsp;
Latifah Show that this has actually led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.800
to some health complications. She developed&nbsp;
a PPD allergy, a condition that can happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:09.060
when you've been dyeing your hair black&nbsp;
for a long time. During filming on NCIS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.855
she woke up with her head swelling&nbsp;
and had to be rushed to the hospital.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.620
"By the time I got to the hospital, half&nbsp;
my head was this big and the other half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.410
was this big, and my eyes were swollen shut,&nbsp;
and I'm like, 'people need to see this.'"

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.100
Afterward, the actor only used black hairspray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.400
right up until she left&nbsp;
NCIS during its 15th season.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.780
Evidently, dyeing her hair black wasn't&nbsp;
the best move for Pauley Perrette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.160
but that's not to say that dyeing her hair&nbsp;
other colors is out of the question. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.980
NCIS — and Abby Sciuto — behind her, she&nbsp;
made the bold choice in 2021 to try out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.600
a brand new look. Instead of choosing just&nbsp;
one hair color, though, she chose multiple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.940
revealing a vibrant rainbow hairstyle in&nbsp;
November of that year. In a Twitter post that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.660
showed off her new, colorful appearance&nbsp;
for the world to see, Perette wrote:

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.840
In the time since debuting this bright hairdo,&nbsp;
she seems to have kept up with it, as her hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.760
has remained that way in a number of subsequent&nbsp;
social media posts. With that, it doesn't look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:12.000
like she has any intention of returning to life&nbsp;
as Abby on NCIS any time soon. And, between her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.580
serious PPD allergy and the tricky nature of the&nbsp;
fame that came with the show, who could blame her?

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:23.160
Yes, it seems that Pauley Perrette is doing&nbsp;
just fine away from NCIS and the Abby Sciuto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.360
role. Maybe someday she'll give both of&nbsp;
them another go, but for the time being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.876
she seems to be enjoying the freedom to do&nbsp;
whatever she'd like — including with her hair.

